<section class="inner-sec">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">How it works on a job site</div>
  <h2>Every call answered, every real job booked</h2>
  <p class="lede">One receptionist covers the phone, the texts, and the website — answering what's routine, screening what's new, and leaving the actual work to you.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Missed-call text-back</strong>A call you can't take on the job becomes a text conversation instead of a voicemail you hear at dinner.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Answers the usuals</strong>Service area, licensed and insured, whether you do that kind of work, rough scheduling windows — answered instantly, any hour.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Screens the job</strong>What's the problem, where's the property, how urgent, owner or renter — captured before it reaches you, so you know if it's worth a truck roll.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Books estimates</strong>Real jobs go straight onto your calendar as estimate appointments — not into a voicemail queue you work through at 8 PM.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Flags real emergencies</strong>A no-heat call in January isn't a Tuesday quote request. Urgent jobs get flagged and routed to you or your on-call right away.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Human handoff</strong>Anything that needs a tradesman's answer — scope, price, code questions — goes to you with a summary of the conversation.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="sec-eyebrow">Who it's built for</div>
  <h2>The trades that run on the phone</h2>
  <p class="lede">If your trade isn't listed — garage doors, tree service, concrete, painting, septic — the fit is the same: if the phone rings while you work, it belongs here.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>HVAC</strong>No-cool in July, no-heat in January. The calls that matter most come after hours — exactly when nobody's in the office to take them.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Plumbing</strong>Burst pipes don't wait for business hours, and neither does the customer calling about one. First answer wins the job.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Electrical</strong>Dead outlets, panel upgrades, remodel rough-ins — screened so you know what's a service call and what's a project before you call back.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Roofing</strong>After a hailstorm the whole valley calls at once. Every caller gets answered while your crews stay on the roof.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>General contractors &amp; remodels</strong>Project inquiries qualified — scope, timeline, budget readiness — before they take an hour of your evening.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Excavation &amp; landscaping</strong>The seasonal rush means the phone rings hardest exactly when you can least afford to stop and answer it.</div>
  </div>
</section>

