<section class="inner-sec" style="padding-top: 10px;">
  <div class="proof-band">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Built for how the trades actually work</div>
    <h2>Answers the phone the way you would</h2>
    <p>A front desk for a trade can't promise what you haven't seen. Yours answers the questions you've approved, books what you've said is bookable, and hands everything else to you — it never bids a job, quotes a price you didn't set, or promises an arrival time you can't keep.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>You set the rules</strong>
        <span>Service area, the work you take, what books directly and what waits for your callback — the receptionist runs on your answers, not its own.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>No prices you didn't approve</strong>
        <span>It shares the pricing you've published — a service-call fee, a free-estimate policy — and nothing else. Bids stay with you.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Emergencies get through</strong>
        <span>You decide what counts as urgent and who gets contacted. Routine work books itself; the real emergencies reach a human fast.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Storm day, same coverage</strong>
        <span>It doesn't get overwhelmed when everyone calls at once. The fiftieth caller of the morning gets the same answer as the first.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

